      },
      "text": "## Examples of Topologies"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nDISCRETE TOPOLOGY: τ = P(X) (all subsets are open).\n  Every set is open. Every set is also closed.\n  Every function from X is continuous (trivially).\n  Metric realization: discrete metric d(x,y) = 0 if x=y, else 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#009",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "INDISCRETE (TRIVIAL) TOPOLOGY: τ = {∅, X}.\n  Only ∅ and X are open.\n  Every function TO X is continuous (f^{-1}(∅)=∅, f^{-1}(X)=domain, both open).\n  Very few functions FROM X are continuous."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#010",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COFINITE TOPOLOGY on X:\n  Open = ∅ or sets with finite complement.\n  Interesting for infinite X: satisfies all axioms.\n  On R: not the same as Euclidean topology. Not Hausdorff!"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#011",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EUCLIDEAN TOPOLOGY on Rⁿ: generated by open balls.\n  The \"standard\" topology of analysis."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#012",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ZARISKI TOPOLOGY on Rⁿ (or kⁿ):\n  Closed sets = algebraic varieties {x : f₁(x)=...=fₖ(x)=0}.\n  Open = complements of varieties.\n  NOT Hausdorff: any two nonempty open sets intersect.\n  Used in algebraic geometry. Fundamentally different from Euclidean."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#013",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ORDER TOPOLOGY on a total order:\n  Generated by rays (a,∞) and (-∞,b).\n  On R: same as Euclidean.\n  On ordinals: gives ordinal topology (interesting for transfinite limits)."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#014",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PRODUCT TOPOLOGY on ∏_{α∈A} Xα:\n  Base = {∏Uα : Uα open in Xα, Uα = Xα for all but finitely many α}.\n  (NOT: all products of open sets — that's the BOX topology, which is finer.)\n  Product topology is the \"right\" one for Tychonoff's theorem.\n  Box topology: {(x₁,x₂,...) : xₙ ∈ Uₙ for all n}. Finer than product.\n```"
    },
