      },
      "text": "SUB-BASE S:\n  Any collection S generates a topology: base = finite intersections of S.\n  Product topology: sub-base = {π_α^{-1}(Uα) : Uα open in Xα}.\n  Tychonoff theorem proves: any product of compact spaces is compact.\n  Proof (Alexander): If X is a product and has an open cover with no finite subcover,\n    restrict to the sub-basic open sets — get a contradiction."
    },
