        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "T₀ (Kolmogorov): For x≠y, ∃ open set containing one but not the other.\nT₁: For x≠y, each is in some open set not containing the other.\n  Equivalently: every singleton {x} is closed.\nT₂ (Hausdorff): Distinct points have disjoint neighborhoods.\n  This is the \"useful\" one — sequences have at most one limit.\nT₃ (Regular + T₁): A closed set and a point not in it have disjoint open sets.\nT₄ (Normal + T₁): Two disjoint closed sets have disjoint open sets.\n  Urysohn's lemma holds. Used to construct partitions of unity."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#026",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:02-topological-spaces, git-history:topology:02-topological-spaces]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "current_path": "topology/02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:topological-spaces",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[topological, spaces]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Topological Spaces",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HIERARCHY: T₄ → T₃ → T₂ → T₁ → T₀."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md#027",
      "path": [
        "02-TOPOLOGICAL-SPACES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
